<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f447caaaf97a5dea87e9d7177d13c9aaccf8887de6e4e99146ac538d2ccc281</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says--83490e71ebdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>French students looking for protests 'to become a major movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91a204b6531cb28520ec7013fb13b5a992bbb307d6a53f35543f43a3ec04b3d6</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:49:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-french-students-looking-for-protests-to-become-a-major-movement--4e68dd5acbe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-french-students-looking-for-protests-to-become-a-major-movement" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of demonstrators marched in cities across France on Tuesday in support of protests by school pupils demanding more education funding, increasing pressure on the government of outgoing President Emmanuel Macron. With teachers and trade unions joining the march, the students are seeking to turn the protests into a "major social movement" to increase pressure on the government, says France 24's Marc Perelman.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: French PM denies 'police repression', suspends classes as clashes erupt at student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ecaa2290f77f0b0ab8060f17cf1fc2eff375315dc0f576bca57417400fce5d4</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:18:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:21:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students--df93e10e4e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students" /></entry><entry><title>'Busification': Inside Ukraine’s controversial recruitment practices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e59e8a9b09288bf523c221ef2d5f3f6843a2c75f9deb6dfbf117f775dcae16e9</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:19:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices--28bf4e6cdcb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices" /><summary type="html">Recent reports and videos of alleged recruitment irregularities are fuelling tensions between mobilisation authorities and Ukrainian society, while raising questions about the oversight and implementation of military recruitment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French students: What do they want?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6354d460f687086655c57c004494e9ade8e8ac2221d90423d53cc59c3e1d9916</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:16:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261006-french-students-what-do-they-want--39b1aa2a286e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261006-french-students-what-do-they-want" /><summary type="html">We take a look at what exactly French high school students are demanding in their nationwide blockades. From crumbling buildings, to absent teachers who are not replaced, to applying to university, we take a look at what has created so much anger among French teens. We also draw parallels between this movement and that of the Yellow Vests.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia 'fears Tigray conflict could get out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfdbbfeb6e95aa699c3125fd39c31eea4ca33ebdca94a8b36e56943f64147a5d</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ethiopia-fears-tigray-conflict-could-get-out-of-control--71887e6b2a41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ethiopia-fears-tigray-conflict-could-get-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">Airstrikes and artillery fire rocked northern Ethiopia's Tigray region overnight into Monday, aid sources said, in clashes between federal government and rebel forces that have raised fears of wider fighting. France 24's Philip Turle says that the Ethiopian government is pushing into Tigray territory amid fears the conflict "could get out of control".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drones kill two, hit fuel hub in one of biggest attacks on Moscow region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49cfdfb93c5de76edc8264ba8d04406087bd09a7bca25592e7e644da15a9e1e</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:07:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukrainian-drones-kill-two-hit-fuel-hub-in-one-of-biggest-attacks-on-moscow-region--ad9c4c4026d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukrainian-drones-kill-two-hit-fuel-hub-in-one-of-biggest-attacks-on-moscow-region" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ​drones killed two people and hit a major fuel depot overnight in one of the biggest attacks of ​the war on Moscow and the surrounding region. France 24's Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>India opposition parties rally for election chief’s exit over voter list changes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d58a3d7d910fcf40d85beb5b4e3bf0de12e5f66a736bdf0c2f7a2aa55a6581b</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:06:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-india-opposition-parties-rally-for-election-chief-s-exit-over-voter-list-changes--652cb77cb918.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-india-opposition-parties-rally-for-election-chief-s-exit-over-voter-list-changes" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties held protests in India’s capital New Delhi on Tuesday, demanding the resignation of the country’s election chief over a contentious revision of voter lists as hundreds of police personnel were deployed across the heart of the city. Tuesday’s demonstration is the latest in a series of near-daily protests beginning last week by student groups, opposition parties and India's “Cockroach” youth movement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Separatists win Quebec election with promise to hold vote on independence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ded52d0fd13f4307a6f51f114d011c6a7b35e7daf835dd3dbbfba7a9626248a1</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:04:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-promise-to-hold-vote-on-independence--4b6d37d7a306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-promise-to-hold-vote-on-independence" /><summary type="html">A separatist party narrowly won Quebec's election on Monday, a result that could make it tougher for Prime Minister Mark Carney to maintain national unity against U.S. President Donald Trump. Provisional results showed the province of 9 million had opted for the Parti Quebecois of Paul St-Pierre Plamondon, which is promising to hold a referendum on breaking ⁠from Canada once Trump leaves office.</summary></entry><entry><title>'They Stole a City' author Lauren Collins on how Wilmington coup was 'covered up'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e3969f8ba91b770d2fc555b8415c6bbb57043193cd489773f2822e13b14707b</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up--81dea464a477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up" /><summary type="html">The author of a new book that tells the story of a White supremacist coup in her hometown of Wilmington, North Carolina has spoken to FRANCE 24 about how those involved and the authorities covered up the event for years. The coup happened back in 1898, but was never mentioned in local schools even when she was a pupil. Lauren Collins is currently living in Paris, where she is a staff journalist for The New Yorker. She spoke to us in Perspective about her book, "They Stole a City".</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>'Heavy police presence' as students set to march in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eed7507d495a8d79261699f326209b66119183a70c3ca534bd3e0d2f9522e637</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:57:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-heavy-police-presence-as-students-set-to-march-in-paris--62f71915fbfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-heavy-police-presence-as-students-set-to-march-in-paris" /><summary type="html">A major march is set to depart from central Paris this afternoon as French students continue their protests classroom conditions. With previous protests marred by violence, France 24’s Claire Paccalin reports that there is already a heave police presence in central Paris as the marchers prepare to get underway.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mexico makes push for fracking despite environmental concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8ef452218c2f5e902687f84a717d01a8820cdc066e8e4d8e0979ba5a5e3e389</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:55:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns--40d4a9cbfcf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns" /><summary type="html">Following months of consultations with energy experts, Mexico is preparing to tap its shale oil and gas reserves using one of the world's most controversial extraction techniques: fracking. The process is already used to extract oil in the southeastern state of Veracruz, where local communities have long complained of pollution and environmental damage. But the administration of President Claudia Sheinbaum is seeking to reduce Mexico's reliance on the United States and – eventually – achieve energy self-sufficiency. FRANCE 24's Quentin Duval and Laurence Cuvillier report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 UK police arrest 22-year-old Briton in suspected Fairford base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d14e70acf7bbe8c9f756973736c9fee952f4025d4364c2534b11a8b7d603494</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:29:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot--cc7e5c5471a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray students relocated by conflict say fled forced conscription</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e34546cfdfdc8cc980d68e4779ec8e78563f138ae2837e0a93d2e400edae868a</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:29:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tigray-students-relocated-by-conflict-say-fled-forced-conscription--e662a3f596af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tigray-students-relocated-by-conflict-say-fled-forced-conscription" /><summary type="html">Due to the ongoing fighting in Ethiopia's Tigray region, some 5,000 students who asked to be relocated are now starting the academic year far from home. Some say back home they faced forced conscription to fight for a cause they didn't believe in. Tom Canetti has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Students protest Cornell's response to gang rape complaint</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e81ab7ae761362bf3e3b9b18341b6f97d53fa65859ff7fc71a772d305ae09aa8</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:26:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-students-protest-cornell-s-response-to-gang-rape-complaint--3353b5e8d47e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-students-protest-cornell-s-response-to-gang-rape-complaint" /><summary type="html">Students at Cornell University staged an anti-rape protest on Monday and to voice their solidarity with ‘Jane Doe’ - the former student who was allegedly ganged raped after consuming drugs and alcohol at a frat house two years ago. Demonstrators called for an inquiry into how the university has handles the matter.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest 22-year-old British man in suspected Fairford base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a422b09c3abb8aebc8c2d5aac9bb22a722f3f2aa0041ad2f3b0d890960d78c5c</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot--cc7e5c5471a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-uk-police-make-new-arrest-in-suspected-air-base-plot" /><summary type="html">UK ​police on Tuesday said they had ​arrested ‌a ⁠22-year ‌old British man ⁠in London on suspicion ​of preparing terrorist acts ‌in relation ​to the suspected plot at the ​RAF ​Fairford ​airbase used ​by the US to strike Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France school protests: Students determined to win 'concessions that mean something'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67e0a994d72b8e338bfd9c751786dc0c898a697636e0f38abe36ade0450c8917</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:24:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-france-school-protests-students-determined-to-win-concessions-that-mean-something--133262a53bf7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-france-school-protests-students-determined-to-win-concessions-that-mean-something" /><summary type="html">Thousands of demonstrators were massing under heavy police surveillance across France on Tuesday, as unions and teachers joined high school students who for days have been demanding better conditions in protests punctuated by violent confrontations. France 24's Luke Shrago reports from outside a Paris high school where he says students he has spoken too remained determined to win concessions from the government.</summary></entry><entry><title>US payroll data shows young workers' jobs most affected by artificial intelligence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4240569a81e063863035449e5a511c2c4b0ce552666c4242939d775effb5bf86</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:15:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261006-us-payroll-data-shows-young-workers-jobs-most-affected-by-artificial-intelligence--b456298f24e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261006-us-payroll-data-shows-young-workers-jobs-most-affected-by-artificial-intelligence" /><summary type="html">In August, US employment in roles most exposed to AI for people aged between 22 and 25 shrank by 4.4 percent year-on-year. This means there's been a contraction every single month since October 2023, about a year after ChatGPT was first released. The high impact of AI on younger workers is one of the key trends emerging from the Canaries Dashboard, a project led by the Stanford Digital Economy Lab and ADP Research. We spoke to ADP Research's Chief Economist Nela Richardson in our Business segment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US, German scientists win Nobel medicine prize for work on light and brain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d249fecb6b4b3316160f00b5dedf54ec253eedf1724bebdd3b2898255be21b5</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:19:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:05:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-us-german-scientists-win-nobel-medicine-prize-for-work-on-light-and-brain--7073689b87e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-us-german-scientists-win-nobel-medicine-prize-for-work-on-light-and-brain" /><summary type="html">American Karl Deisseroth and Germans Peter Hegemann and Georg Nagel won the 2026 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine ​on Monday for developing optogenetics, a technique that uses light to control individual nerve cells in the brain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Philip Ingram sees Russia, China and Iran stepping up ‘gray zone’ activities across UK and Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e77f55cbacdcb01f60da6208c51b1a1ddb8bae7e781ab97ff87d4d754ef96291</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:13:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261006-philip-ingram-sees-russia-china-and-iran-stepping-up-gray-zone-activities-across-uk-and-eur--f068b3b762fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261006-philip-ingram-sees-russia-china-and-iran-stepping-up-gray-zone-activities-across-uk-and-europe" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Philip Ingram, journalist and former British military intelligence officer. The events surrounding RAF Fairford are not an isolated incident, explains Ingram. It's part of a much wider security issue in which conventional military operations, intelligence activity and gray-zone tactics increasingly overlap.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Student protests: First images from demonstrations in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0a2a65654d5abcb0fce27777119b654cc91414eca95a0a14c495da2a9752ba7</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-student-protests-first-images-from-demonstrations-in-paris--883b0567e88e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-student-protests-first-images-from-demonstrations-in-paris" /><summary type="html">France braced on Tuesday for a day of nationwide high-school ​blockades and trade union-led street protests in support of students demanding that President Emmanuel Macron's cash-strapped government tackle understaffed and dilapidated schools.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Thousands of students march across France as clashes reported in Lyon and Strasbourg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac0b249f3a103e49793e0081a1df9eacc36bd7c70eea95b6649a0d4c5b0051b</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:18:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:40:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students--df93e10e4e3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students" /></entry><entry><title>Should we be worried about a plague outbreak in Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e589ed275b31f3176e0a91aa124255d7569f53bca6de64ee754512aca705e92</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:30:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia--38fad56138a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261006-should-we-be-worried-about-a-plague-outbreak-in-russia" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 6: The death of a researcher in Siberia, reportedly from the plague, sparks concern despite Russian authorities' denial. But first: French high school protesters are promising "Act 3" of their protest movement against learning conditions. Also, Le Monde speaks to the editor of Russian independent outlet Novaya Gazeta ahead of the 20th anniversary of the murder of investigative journalist Anna Politkovskaya. Finally, it appears that butter is back in fashion.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria searches for missing crew as drones hit two Black Sea ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc48f30ec16f71371b3c00328e8eae0b6ec7d968c873b850980e5f5a20f7628d</id><updated>2026-10-06T15:20:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:24:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships--a9c664076180.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-bulgaria-searches-for-missing-crew-as-drones-hit-two-more-black-sea-ships" /><summary type="html">Bulgarian authorities on Tuesday launched a search for missing crew members of a boat that sank in its economic zone in the Black Sea after drones hit two merchant vessels. Black Sea shipping has been hit by growing fallout from the war in Ukraine in recent months.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
